y over Bernard Taylor and is campaigning on cost of living and clean water, but he has raised under $600,000 and holds modest cash reserves.\n\nNo public general-election polling is available, so the picture rests on district fundamentals, money, and expert assessments. Rating outlets uniformly call the race for Republicans, with most rating it Safe or Solid R, and prediction markets give Democrats roughly a one-in-ten chance. The race is rated Likely Republican, with an expected Republican margin in the low double digits.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.066, "margin": -9.63}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.058, "margin": -11.0}]}